WEBVTT

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.220
To the rhythm!

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.250
Check it!

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.330
OK, fellas!

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.580
Yeah yeah party people
let's go let's turn it up

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.360
Let's rush in let's send it flying
let's attack let's dash

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.090
The battlefields are sacred,
Bakuretsu Tenshi, Crazy Burst Angel

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:32.820
They're a bother, they're cheeky,
come on, blast 'em good!

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.200
Everybody, loosey

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.870
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.410
Vividly, crazy

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.710
Fly up, angel

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.880
We are the risma so charisma

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.050
We soar, really prisma (bomber)

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.550
Hey! It's danceable OK
shake it right now let's go

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.520
Gutsiness let's go beat
let's ride the rhythm tension

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.920
It goes flying frustration

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.160
Alright let's go let's get it on
loosey beauty get your body

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.430
Everybody, loosey

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:10.170
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.500
Vividly, crazy

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.500
Fly up, angel

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:38.990
Stop screwin' around! Pay up!

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:42.790
Shut up! I'd never pay a fraud like you!

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:47.300
--Drop the tough act, old man!
--Ha! You don't have the guts!

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.330
What?! Don't you mock me!

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.340
You're getting' on my nerves, kid!

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:56.640
--Shut up! I'll kill ya!
--Why, you...!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.420
What the...?!

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.950
Gunshots out of nowhere!

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:16.190
Machine guns on both sides!
I thought for sure I was dead...

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:20.460
Now that people can legally own weapons,

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:25.160
guns on the market keep
getting stronger and stronger.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:29.690
I figured we'd be safer with
the RAPT headquarters here.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:34.870
Apprehension rates are on the rise,
but arrests are on the decline.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:39.090
Apprehension is up
but arrests are down? How come?

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:44.330
Fewer people are being caught alive.
All thanks to RAPT.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:47.600
Kyohei-<i>kun</i>. I hear you're
looking for another job?

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:50.430
Yes. I quit my last one...

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.670
A job is fine and all,
but don't be missing class now.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:58.580
--Of course not.
--Sensei. What's that?

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.810
Oh, this?

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.320
A job offer off the Internet.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.990
But there've been
lots of pranks lately, so...

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:12.360
"Eagerly seeking a wonderful man
to cook delicious and fancy cuisine.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:18.660
Excellent salary and conditions.
First come basis. Visit now!"

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.300
Is this for real?!

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.270
"Skyscraper Gangster Story"

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:27.570
--<i>He finally left New Alcatraz
Prison after 10 long years.</i>
--The air on the outside's great...

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.640
--<i>What awaited him was a cruel reality!</i>
--Father!
--Boss!

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.610
--<i>A torn bond... Betrayal...</i>
--Sister!
--Avenge his death!

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.650
--<i>A heated fight begins
between the two men!</i>
--Why, you...!

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.650
--<i>A heated fight begins
between the two men!</i>
--Stop. It's pointless.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.450
--<i>Starring Machikata Hiroki
and Kiba Shinichi!</i>
--A fight it is!

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:40.650
--<i>Starring Machikata Hiroki
and Kiba Shinichi!</i>
--Bring it on!

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:45.320
--<i>The heroine between them is
Hollywood actress, Yuka Salmon!</i>
--Stop!

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:48.950
--<i>A shocking suspense love comedy!
Watch for it!</i>
--Aaah!

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.860
Here is the news.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:56.970
Late last night,
a freight car was attacked

00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:00.040
by an unregistered workbot
on the Tomei Mega Highway

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.910
and had its construction
materials stolen.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:07.080
Four similar events
have occurred this month.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.710
The investigation has changed hands
and is under RAPT jurisdiction.

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:22.860
Tachibana Kyohei-<i>san</i> from
Love & Happy Cooking School?

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.890
Yes. That's right...

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:31.100
You're saving money to study abroad?

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.100
I'm studying to be a patissier.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:38.180
Oh, that's a pastry chef.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:42.310
Patissier? Never heard of that.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:47.420
On-the-job training is the only
way to break into the business.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:51.760
But it costs a lot of taxes
to go overseas nowadays.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.360
I can't ask my parents, so...

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:59.630
Remarkable! You have a real goal
even though you're young.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.160
I like people like that.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:10.240
Pastries are my specialty,
but I have some experience

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.940
with Japanese, Western,
Chinese, and Italian food too.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.010
I think there's an extra zero here...

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:24.520
--Yes?
--Sei? Where are you?

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:27.420
Buying food with the new cook.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.550
We'll be there soon, hold on.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.860
Hurry! I'm starving...!

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.370
--Let's hurry.
--Okay...

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:44.310
How many people am I cooking for?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.840
Is it a big mansion or something?

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.310
Something like that.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.980
Our last cook suddenly
had to return home.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:56.880
Here?

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:06.790
--It's Sei! I brought our new cook!
--Coming!

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:21.210
Welcome back! Is he our new cook?

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:24.770
--That's right.
--Hello...

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:57.010
This is where you'll work. Your job
is to cook meals for these girls.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:02.850
Do they go for picnics in this?

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:06.760
No, this is their home.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:08.560
We all live here.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.760
All? Your families too?

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:15.000
Leave 'em alone and they
eat nothing but junk food.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:19.740
We need a chef who will
cook them real meals.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.170
That's Meg.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:24.110
This is Amy.

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:26.140
Turn around.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:30.280
--Turn. 180 degrees.
--Alright...

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:31.770
Like this?

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:35.250
Isn't he too young?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:41.660
Don't be rude. He's an excellent
cook from a real cooking school.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.700
I wouldn't say 'excellent'...

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:50.300
--You smell like cake!
--I just baked a practice one...

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:53.540
Say! That flyer was cute, wasn't it?

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.310
You drew that?

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:58.540
Yup! I was worried who'd show up,

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.210
but I'm glad it was someone interesting!

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:05.080
You look like you'd last a
while even in bad situations!

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:11.920
I dunno. He looks kinda
wimpy and wiry if you ask me.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:14.890
Kyohei-<i>san</i> is saving
money to study overseas.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:19.590
Wouldn't it be nice to help
make his dream come true?

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:25.740
You, helping someone?

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.810
To make his dream come true?
That's hilarious!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.710
Sei! Has your comedic edge
gotten sharper?

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:37.180
Don't mind them. Well?
Are you up to the job?

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:41.190
Yes, of course! If you'd like me to!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.960
Hold on! What about Jo's say in this?!

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.420
--Jo?
--She's here?

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:53.060
She just got back.
Said she did some job for free.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.570
I bet she's watching
another video somewhere.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:58.160
She always does after a job.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.700
There she is!

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.870
Just a sec!

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:04.710
Look away.

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:08.270
Is 'eh' and 'huh' all you say?!

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:12.880
I'm sorry.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:17.050
She has a sharp tongue
but she's really a kind person.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:18.890
Meg? Kind?

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:23.060
Your jokes really are good today!

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:26.830
Um... Are you all sisters?

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:31.960
No. We just wound up together.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:43.680
Jo. This is the new cook.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.440
Think we can use him?

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.180
A man?

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:52.360
Sure, whatever.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:57.630
That settles it. Welcome aboard,
Tachibana Kyohei-<i>kun</i>.

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:59.530
Thanks...

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:05.600
Sorry. I'll be right back.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:21.220
Say, are you--

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:23.320
Hey, now!

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:26.120
You're not trying to make a
pass at her already, are you?!

00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:28.350
No!

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.490
<i>She couldn't be...</i>

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.370
"Acquire Data Disc"

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.470
We got a job. Everyone, get ready.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:48.880
--A job?
--Eh? But I'm so hungry...!

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.620
Don't be selfish. What are we here for?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:56.120
Once the job's done, we can
buy the parts you wanted.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:15:00.360
Really? Let's get to work, then! Work!

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:03.190
Um... About my job...

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:07.760
I'm really sorry. Could you
possibly leave for today?

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:11.160
Jo. We got a job.

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:14.840
Jo! Stop!

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:17.070
You! Get out already!

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.710
Please come back after school tomorrow.

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.510
--Okay...
--Later, then.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.550
Quit your dawdling and scram!

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.090
Makes no sense at all...

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:43.430
<i>I wonder if they're really rich?
How are they related?</i>

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:45.900
<i>They're all good-looking,
but something seems off...</i>

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.890
<i>What exactly do they do...?</i>

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.440
What are you--

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:12.660
Say. What would that boy think
if he learned what we do?

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:17.220
He'd run off. He looked
like a total wimp.

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:21.030
--Jo! Are you ready?
--OK.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.170
The job is simple.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:28.080
Weapon smugglers are making
a deal in a Harumi warehouse.

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:31.380
Our target is the disc they're trading.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.880
What's on the disc?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:37.980
Not sure. Maybe Bailan wants
to copy it and mass market it.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:41.190
A car's been following us.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:44.180
Transmitting an aerial view now.

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.770
We have company? What do we do?

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:52.100
We can't cause a scene here.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:55.090
Let's leave it alone.
It can't do anything anyway.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:11.020
The info was right.
The deal's going down right now.

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.620
Good. Get to work.

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:15.930
Can we take care of 'em all?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.600
No. Don't cause a scene.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:19.860
Keep things quiet.

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.770
--Confirmed.
--Same here.

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:37.140
--What the...?!
--A mouse?!

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.750
Damn thing!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.790
Don't move!

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.520
Behind you, too!

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:53.760
--Aren't we just after the disc?
--This is bonus.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:07.010
Bailan conspirators.
We knew you were after the disc.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.250
Too bad, though.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:12.680
We took one of your friends
for just such an occasion.

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:15.090
Friend? Who?

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:18.520
--Did Sei screw up?
--Never!

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:22.490
--What's he doing here?!
--Who is he?

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.480
That cook!

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:33.960
Return the case. Otherwise,
his brain gets splattered all over!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.470
--Go ahead.
--What?!

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.980
You sure?

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:49.680
I swear I'll shoot!

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.030
Go ahead.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.910
What?! Nobody told me about that!

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:15.780
Doesn't matter! Now's our chance!

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:19.540
What the heck's going on?!

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.950
--Stay with me!
--Right...

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:43.300
Meg!

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:01.060
--Hot...!
--Don't move!

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:02.180
Don't shoot!

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:07.590
--Escape on your own! Okay?!
--T-Thanks...

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.490
Meg!

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:22.440
--Meg! Get down from there!
--No! I can't break loose!

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:26.520
Meg! What's going on?! Tell me!

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.220
What's that cybot?! Report!

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:31.860
--You don't know either?!
--It's an enemy, whatever it is.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:35.120
Meg's been caught. Release Django!

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.230
Jo!

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:04.920
Wake up, Django!

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.460
Jo's waiting for you!

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:25.840
Don't get too smug,
you bucket of bolts!

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.910
She's the one I saw in Shinjuku...!

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:34.850
I'll take you...!

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:39.590
Take you to Hell!

00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:05.640
I remained motionless within the crowd

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:13.120
Not even the voice of my
tears carried on this street

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:20.930
as my feelings of lonesomeness joined it

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:30.230
In truth, everyone wants
to smile with each other,

00:22:30.230 --> 00:22:36.810
yet they get hurt
when they can't do it very well

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:45.780
But someone will always
be there to watch,

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:53.190
so let's walk together
beneath this sky

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:16.780
<i>Meg has been abducted by a mysterious
cybot that suddenly appeared.</i>

00:23:16.780 --> 00:23:19.120
<i>Kyohei is made part of her rescue plan,</i>

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:22.390
<i>and with Jo, he enters
the lawless town of Shibuya</i>

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:27.220
<i>On the next Burst Angel--</i>
"The Coldhearted Gunfighter"
